        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-23T14:20:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As someone who is an IT person and in other contexts generally considers himself to be quite tech savvy, but has had to ask migrantp for help on many occassions when trying to figure out how to get to playtester content in Steam and/or Android, I think we should give ourselves a bit of a break when dealing with technologies/areas infrequently. I only have one other android game on my phone and no other ones on Steam. I usually have to relearn the interface for doing anything on these platforms when the SotM content needs to be updated, and I find the Steam interfaces particularly challenging to navigate. First I have to get past the fact that there is both an application interface and a web interface, then I find the series of menu options and popups byzantine, and all of this is in the context of not being familiar with the lingo and tasks. If the steps I need to take aren't laid out in precise detail, I find it very easy to get lost.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
