      {
        "id": 196699,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-23T17:55:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think the problem with Android and Steam specifically are that they're designed mostly by geeks.</p><p>Totally serious. I find that geeks have a really bad time with both providing sparse inadequate documentation and creating confusing UIs because they/we forget that not everyone has every programming language/shortcut/way of doing things memorized.</p><p>Yes, I obviously say this self-depreciatingly AS a geek myself, but I've spent my whole life basically in a blue-collar culture area and around people who don't really understand tech so I have a foot in both worlds. Don't get me started on the jargon we geeks think up, either. I've had so many non-geeks go \"OH, is it really that simple? I never realized,\" regards geek concepts whenever I take the time to translate from Geek to English.</p>",
